.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt CBLINK 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cblink
.Nd netlink-style messaging over CBOR between userland programs
.Sh LIBRARY
cblink Library
.Pq libcblink , Fl lcblink
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In cblink.h
.In cbl_schema.h
.Pp
Link with
.Fl lcblink ,
or use
.Xr pkg-config 1
with the package
.Ql cblink .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library carries netlink-style messages between programs: a fixed binary
header with a family, a command, flags, a sequence number and a stream
id, followed by a body that is one CBOR map
.Pq RFC 8949 :
its keys are the SIDs
.Pq RFC 9595
of YANG nodes, its values those nodes' data in YANG-CBOR
.Pq RFC 9254 .
Servers serve the YANG modules they implement by SID, through the
built-in YANG family, or register
.Em families
of operations of their own; clients send requests, iterate dumps, open
flow-controlled streams and subscribe to notifications.
The same library serves both sides.
.Pp
Messages travel over TCP, SCTP and
.Ux Ns -domain
sockets.
TCP uses TLS 1.3 and SCTP uses DTLS 1.2
.Pq RFC 6083 ,
when OpenSSL was built with SCTP support, as the base system's is
.Po
.Fn cbl_features
reports
.Dv CBL_FEAT_DTLS_SCTP
.Pc ;
both ends present certificates
.Pq mutual TLS
unless plaintext is explicitly requested with
.Dv CBL_PLAINTEXT .
.Nm
contains no HTTP implementation; behind a load balancer it runs under a
TCP proxy with TLS passthrough,
optionally with the PROXY protocol.
.Pp
The wire format, the full API, the YANG that
.Xr cblink-gen 1
takes and the transports are described in
.Pa docs/WIRE-FORMAT.md ,
.Pa docs/API.md ,
.Pa docs/YANG.md
and
.Pa docs/TRANSPORTS.md ,
installed under
.Pa ${PREFIX}/share/doc/cblink
by the port.
Programs describe their data, rpcs and notifications in YANG modules and
let
.Xr cblink-gen 1
generate the structs, the schema tables, the helpers that put them in
messages and read them back, and the server's handler table.
.Ss Conventions
All types are opaque.
Functions that can fail return 0 or an
.Xr errno 2
value; they do not set
.Va errno .
Objects whose creation fails are not created.
A function that sends a message consumes it, also on failure, with one
exception:
.Fn cbl_stream_send
returning
.Er EAGAIN
leaves the message to the caller, to send again later or to free.
.Pp
Each received message owns an arena; strings, byte strings and structures
parsed from it point into the message and live until
.Fn cbl_msg_free .
Building a message records the first error and makes later calls on that
message no-ops; the error is returned when the message is sent or by
.Fn cbl_msg_error .
.Ss Contexts
.Fn cbl_ctx_new
creates a context: the family registry, default limits, default TLS
configuration and multicast groups.
The library has no global mutable state; independent contexts may be used
in one process.
.Fn cbl_ctx_set_limit
changes a limit before the first listener or connection uses the
context
.Pq see Sx LIMITS .
.Fn cbl_ctx_free
fails with
.Er EBUSY
while a loop, listener or connection made from the context exists.
.Fn cbl_tls_reload
rereads certificates, keys, CAs and CRLs for the connections made from
then on.
.Ss Messages and bodies
.Fn cbl_msg_new
starts a message for a family and command.
A body's top-level items are added by SID:
.Fn cbl_msg_put_ynode
puts a node's struct as YANG-CBOR,
.Fn cbl_msg_put_ymember
a module's top-level node from the module's struct,
.Fn cbl_msg_put_ynull
a null, and
.Fn cbl_msg_put_sid_raw
a value already encoded.
An rpc's or an action's input and output go under the rpc's or the
action's SID.
.Xr cblink-gen 1
writes typed helpers for each struct over these.
.Pp
On a received message,
.Fn cbl_msg_sid_raw
finds an item's bytes by its SID,
.Fn cbl_msg_ydecode
and
.Fn cbl_msg_ydecode_member
decode it into its struct.
The decoder has checked the whole body first: definite lengths, integer
keys, no key twice, YANG-CBOR's tags only where they may be, and the
limits.
.Pp
An ERROR frame, or an ack with a warning or a cookie, carries the
cblink module's
.Em error
structure, built with
.Fn cbl_msg_put_error
and
.Fn cbl_msg_put_cookie
and read with
.Fn cbl_msg_err_code
.Pq its errno ,
.Fn cbl_msg_err_str ,
.Fn cbl_msg_err_path ,
.Fn cbl_msg_err_miss_type ,
.Fn cbl_msg_err_sid
.Pq the node at fault
and
.Fn cbl_msg_err_cookie .
.Pp
.Fn cbl_msg_encode
and
.Fn cbl_frame_decode
convert between messages and raw frames for programs that carry frames
themselves.
.Ss Families and servers
A server with operations of its own describes a family with a
.Vt struct cbl_family_def :
its name, version, operations and multicast groups, and registers it with
.Fn cbl_family_register .
The family id is assigned at registration; clients learn it by name with
.Fn cbl_resolve .
Family 0 is the built-in control family, the YANG module
.Ql cblink-ctrl ,
which answers name lookups, subscriptions, pings and hellos.
.Pp
Family 1, the YANG family, serves the modules of the server tables
.Xr cblink-gen 1
writes
.Pq Fl m Cm server
once
.Fn cbl_yserver_add
is given one: GET reads top-level data nodes, a dump a node a frame;
EDIT creates, replaces and deletes them, all or nothing; RPC calls an
rpc; GET-SID sends the modules'
.Pa .sid
files.
The handlers the server defines get the argument given with
.Fn cbl_req_yarg ,
and name the node at fault with
.Fn cbl_req_set_yerr .
.Fn cbl_msg_put_yget
puts a GET's targets.
.Pp
An operation's handler receives a
.Vt cbl_req
and answers with
.Fn cbl_req_reply_new
and
.Fn cbl_req_send ,
or returns an error, optionally described with
.Fn cbl_req_set_err .
.Fn cbl_req_defer
keeps a request open after the handler returns, to be finished later with
.Fn cbl_req_complete .
If its connection goes away first, the request is cancelled
.Pq Fn cbl_req_cancelled , Fn cbl_req_set_cancel .
A stream open may be deferred too, and accepted later from any thread.
Dump handlers return one item per call with
.Fn cbl_req_dump_item
and are called again while the client keeps up.
Operations flagged
.Dv CBL_OPF_AUTH
run only for an authenticated peer.
.Ss Endpoints
Endpoints are named by URIs:
.Bl -tag -width "unix:path" -offset indent
.It Li tcp:// Ns Ar host : Ns Ar port
TCP with TLS 1.3.
.It Li sctp:// Ns Ar host Ns Op , Ns Ar host ... : Ns Ar port
SCTP with DTLS 1.2; several hosts give a multihomed association.
.It Li unix: Ns Ar path
A
.Ux Ns -domain
stream socket; peers are identified by
.Xr getpeereid 3 .
.El
.Pp
.Fn cbl_listener_new
and
.Fn cbl_listener_start
accept connections;
.Fn cbl_conn_new
and
.Fn cbl_conn_connect
open one.
TLS is configured with a
.Vt cbl_tls
.Pq Fn cbl_tls_new , Fn cbl_tls_set_cert , Fn cbl_tls_set_ca , Fn cbl_tls_set_crl ,
set on the context, a listener or a connection.
Starting a TCP or SCTP endpoint without TLS fails with
.Er EPERM
unless it was created with
.Dv CBL_PLAINTEXT .
A TCP listener created with
.Dv CBL_LF_PROXY
expects every connection to start with a PROXY protocol header, version
1 or 2, from a proxy in front of it, and reports the client address that
header names
.Pq Dv CBL_PEER_PROXIED .
.Fn cbl_listener_add_proxy
limits who may send that header.
.Ss Peer identity
.Fn cbl_req_peer
and
.Fn cbl_conn_peer
describe the other side the same way on every transport:
.Fn cbl_peer_subject ,
.Fn cbl_peer_issuer ,
.Fn cbl_peer_san
and
.Fn cbl_peer_fingerprint
for certificates,
.Fn cbl_peer_cred
for local peers, and
.Fn cbl_peer_flags ,
which says whether the peer is authenticated
.Pq Dv CBL_PEER_AUTHENTICATED .
.Ss Requests, dumps, notifications and streams
.Fn cbl_request
sends a request and waits for its reply;
.Fn cbl_request_async
calls a function instead.
On a loop thread, where the synchronous calls fail with
.Er EDEADLK ,
.Fn cbl_resolve_async ,
.Fn cbl_subscribe_async
and the generated asynchronous wrappers are used instead.
.Fn cbl_dump_start
and
.Fn cbl_dump_next
iterate the items of a dump.
.Fn cbl_subscribe
joins a multicast group of a family; the server sends to it with
.Fn cbl_notify ,
or to one peer with
.Fn cbl_conn_notify ;
.Fn cbl_conn_subscribed
says whether a peer joined, for what is told only to those that asked.
A YANG notification goes to the YANG family's group
.Ql notify
with
.Fn cbl_ynotify ;
.Fn cbl_msg_ynotif
tells a receiver which it is, when it happened and its content.
.Pp
Streams carry a sequence of messages in one or both directions with
credit-based flow control:
.Fn cbl_stream_open
on the client,
.Fn cbl_stream_accept
in the server's open handler,
.Fn cbl_stream_send ,
.Fn cbl_stream_half_close ,
.Fn cbl_stream_close
and
.Fn cbl_stream_reset .
A sender that runs out of credit gets
.Er EAGAIN
and is called back through
.Fa on_writable
when the receiver grants more.
A thread that may call a stream after it ended holds it with
.Fn cbl_stream_ref
and
.Fn cbl_stream_rele ;
such calls fail with
.Er EPIPE .
.Ss Event loop and integration
A
.Vt cbl_loop
runs connections, listeners, timers and signals on one thread with
.Xr kqueue 2 :
.Fn cbl_loop_run ,
.Fn cbl_loop_timer ,
.Fn cbl_loop_signal ,
.Fn cbl_loop_post .
Callbacks for a connection run on its loop's thread.
Programs with their own event loop use
.Fn cbl_conn_fd ,
.Fn cbl_conn_interest
and
.Fn cbl_conn_process
instead.
A connection on no loop drives its socket itself inside
.Fn cbl_request ,
which makes simple blocking clients short.
.Fn cbl_conn_stats
reports what a connection is doing: queued output, requests in flight,
dropped notifications.
.Ss YANG schema tables
.In cbl_schema.h
describes the schema tables
.Xr cblink-gen 1
writes of YANG modules
.Pq Fl m Cm schema :
every node with its SID
.Pq RFC 9595 ,
its type, its children by SID, its constraints and expressions; the
identities a value may name, each with those derived from it; each
module's features.
.Fn cbl_ynode_child
finds the child a map key's delta names
.Pq RFC 9254 ,
.Fn cbl_yschema_node
and
.Fn cbl_yschema_ident
a node and an identity by SID, and
.Fn cbl_yderived_from
answers XPath's
.Fn derived-from
and, with
.Fa self ,
.Fn derived-from-or-self .
.Fn cbl_yencode
writes a node's value from the struct
.Xr cblink-gen 1
made for it as YANG-CBOR
.Pq RFC 9254 ,
its children keyed by their SID deltas, into a
.Vt struct cbl_ybuf ;
.Fn cbl_ydecode
reads it back into such a struct, what it points to allocated from a
.Vt cbl_yarena
.Pq Fn cbl_yarena_new , Fn cbl_yarena_free ,
and with
.Dv CBL_YD_STRICT
refuses a key the node has no child for.
A list entry may be one byte of input and a struct of many: what an
arena holds is bounded,
.Fn cbl_yarena_set_limit ,
64 MiB unless set, and a decode past it fails with
.Er ENOMEM .
It checks what the CBOR is, not what the schema further says.
.Sh LIMITS
Every limit has a default, a minimum and a maximum, and applies per
context, listener or connection
.Pq Fn cbl_ctx_set_limit , Fn cbl_listener_set_limit , Fn cbl_conn_set_limit .
Limits on input are checked before memory is allocated for it.
They include the largest frame
.Pq Dv CBL_LIM_MAX_FRAME ,
nesting depth, values per body, open streams per connection, the initial
stream window, outstanding requests, connections, and handshake and
idle timeouts.
A server stops reading a peer whose replies pile up in its send queue,
rather than dropping them; a peer that stays quiet is sent keepalive
pings, and one that does not answer them is dropped after the idle
timeout.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Vt int
return 0 on success and an
.Xr errno 2
value on failure; among them
.Bl -tag -width "EOPNOTSUPP"
.It Bq Er EAGAIN
A stream has no credit; try again from
.Fa on_writable .
.It Bq Er EACCES
The operation needs an authenticated peer.
.It Bq Er EMSGSIZE
A message is larger than the peer or the transport accepts.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
No such family, group or node.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The family has no such operation, or the operation does not support
dumps.
.It Bq Er EPERM
TLS is required and was not configured.
.It Bq Er ETIMEDOUT
No reply in time.
.El
.Pp
When a request fails at the server, the reply's extended ack says why.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A client of the module
.Pa kv@2026-10-13.yang ,
its store read and an rpc called through the YANG family, with what
.Xr cblink-gen 1
writes into
.Pa kv.h
and
.Pa kv_schema.c :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <cblink.h>
#include <cbl_schema.h>
#include "kv.h"

struct kv_clear_input in = { .prefix = "tmp/" };
struct kv_clear_output out;
cbl_ctx *ctx;
cbl_conn *conn;
cbl_msg *m, *r;
cbl_yarena *a;
struct kv_store st;
int error;

if ((error = cbl_ctx_new(&ctx)) != 0 ||
    (error = cbl_conn_new(ctx, "unix:/var/run/kv.sock", 0, &conn)) != 0 ||
    (error = cbl_conn_connect(conn)) != 0)
	errc(1, error, "kv");
a = cbl_yarena_new();
/* A GET without targets: the whole datastore. */
cbl_msg_new(ctx, CBL_YANG_FAMILY, CBL_YCMD_GET, 0, &m);
if ((error = cbl_request(conn, m, &r, -1)) != 0 ||
    (error = kv_store_parse(r, &st, a, CBL_YD_STRICT, NULL, 0)) != 0)
	errc(1, error, "get");
printf("%zu entries\en", st.entry.n);
if ((error = kv_clear_call(conn, &in, &out, a, -1)) != 0)
	errc(1, error, "clear");
.Ed
.Pp
Complete servers and clients are installed by the port under
.Pa ${PREFIX}/share/examples/cblink .
