.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Every frame is untrusted input: headers are checked before any
allocation, CBOR bodies are decoded with fixed limits on size, depth and
item count, and only definite-length CBOR with integer keys is accepted,
its only tags YANG-CBOR's (4, and 43 to 47, each on the kind of value it
belongs to).
The YANG codec checks UTF-8, bounds what a decode may allocate
.Pq Fn cbl_yarena_set_limit
and, with
.Dv CBL_YD_STRICT ,
refuses a key the node has no child for.
.Pp
Plaintext must be requested explicitly.
A
.Dv CBL_LF_PROXY
listener believes the address in the PROXY header, so it must be
reachable only through the proxy; the header never makes a peer
authenticated.
